1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,880
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:33,960
(Based on the novel
Doctor Qin: Executer)

3
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,600
You're so beautiful.

4
00:00:42,759 --> 00:00:44,000
It's about time.

5
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:46,320
Let's go.

6
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,799
Keke.

7
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,840
Be a good girl. Go.

8
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,079
You're still young.

9
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:34,079
You can start over.

10
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:35,959
Don't worry about me.

11
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,680
There's food and shelter in prison.

12
00:01:39,719 --> 00:01:40,519
Qin Ming

13
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:44,480
is just a beautiful memory in your life.

14
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:55,879
Can you hug me?

15
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,640
I never had a mom.

16
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,199
Before I met you,

17
00:02:09,319 --> 00:02:10,960
I never felt a mother's love.

18
00:02:13,199 --> 00:02:14,080
Thank you

19
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:17,360
for giving me the best years of my life.

20
00:02:27,759 --> 00:02:28,560
Keke.

21
00:02:30,199 --> 00:02:32,240
I won't let you do anything dangerous.

22
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:56,400
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 27=

23
00:02:57,719 --> 00:02:58,520
(Qin.)

24
00:02:58,759 --> 00:03:01,080
(Jin Keke just killed herself
at the hospital.)

25
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:02,960
(She's in emergency care now.)

26
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,199
(Are you with Song Yalan?)

27
00:03:06,319 --> 00:03:07,680
(Han Liang and the team
are almost there.)

28
00:03:27,919 --> 00:03:28,759
Ziyan, Ou Wen, come with me.

29
00:03:28,759 --> 00:03:29,759
Everyone else, split up.

30
00:03:29,759 --> 00:03:30,400
Yes, sir.

31
00:03:34,199 --> 00:03:35,000
Qin Ming.

32
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,280
You said I'm cruel.

33
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,360
Fine.

34
00:03:40,439 --> 00:03:42,199
Let me tell you why.

35
00:03:42,919 --> 00:03:43,800
Some debts

36
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,919
can only be paid with despair.

37
00:03:48,759 --> 00:03:50,240
What I owe Wen,

38
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,759
what Jin Keke owes Wen,

39
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:54,919
and what everyone owes Wen

40
00:03:55,879 --> 00:03:58,599
are going to be settled today.

41
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,040
(Base, tomorrow at 8 PM. Detective Ming)

42
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,080
Mom!

43
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:06,960
Can you respect my privacy?

44
00:04:11,159 --> 00:04:13,840
Qin Ming's handwriting is pretty neat.

45
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:15,840
Mom, it's not what you think.

46
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:18,879
This is for Keke.

47
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:20,519
She was doing homework here today

48
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:21,480
and left it here.

49
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:25,040
So I misunderstood.

50
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:38,839
Mom...

51
00:04:39,879 --> 00:04:41,040
No asking about this?

52
00:04:43,279 --> 00:04:44,120
Ask what?

53
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:46,639
If you want to tell me,

54
00:04:46,639 --> 00:04:48,360
you'll tell me on your own.

55
00:04:49,079 --> 00:04:50,279
If you don't want to,

56
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,879
asking will just upset you.

57
00:04:55,839 --> 00:04:57,600
But tell me the truth.

58
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,879
Do you kind of like Qin Ming?

59
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:04,519
Mom, what are you saying?

60
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,399
What's the big deal?

61
00:05:07,839 --> 00:05:09,199
You're almost grown up.

62
00:05:09,519 --> 00:05:11,279
It's natural to like someone.

63
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:15,199
But remember.

64
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:18,319
Whoever you like, or whoever likes you,

65
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:19,920
first and foremost,

66
00:05:20,399 --> 00:05:21,480
you're Xia Wen.

67
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,720
And then,

68
00:05:24,319 --> 00:05:26,639
you're someone's friend or classmate.

69
00:05:26,959 --> 00:05:28,920
Don't rush to label yourself.

70
00:05:31,959 --> 00:05:33,680
Mom, you sound so old-fashioned.

71
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:38,879
So what if I'm? It works.

72
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:42,639
Got it.

73
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:47,800
"Detective Ming..."

74
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:49,439
Mom!

75
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,680
(New Message To: Mom)

76
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,959
(Mom, Keke is in some trouble.)

77
00:05:57,959 --> 00:05:59,680
(I've decided to go help her.)

78
00:06:09,639 --> 00:06:11,639
Wen was too kind.

79
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:15,399
She risked everything for Jin Keke.

80
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,639
But what about you, Qin Ming?

81
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:21,560
If that afternoon,

82
00:06:21,759 --> 00:06:22,920
you had asked them

83
00:06:23,199 --> 00:06:25,920
where they were headed,
what they were up to,

84
00:06:27,319 --> 00:06:31,399
would she have missed that bus?

85
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:36,079
Would she have missed that rainy night?

86
00:06:37,519 --> 00:06:39,759
Would she still be alive?

87
00:06:47,879 --> 00:06:48,680
Qin Ming,

88
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:51,519
I'm not blaming you.

89
00:06:56,199 --> 00:06:57,800
I just often recall

90
00:06:58,879 --> 00:07:00,959
this pain of losing my daughter.

91
00:07:04,319 --> 00:07:06,199
I don't know who to blame.

92
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:15,759
But what truly keeps me awake at night

93
00:07:17,519 --> 00:07:18,279
is that

94
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:21,839
I'm the one who made it happen.

95
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:30,240
(Good girl.)

96
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,759
(I'm proud of you.)

97
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:38,600
Qin Ming.

98
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:41,480
Haven't you been looking for the killer?

99
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,240
The killer's right in front of you now,

100
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,959
an open-minded and proud mother

101
00:07:48,399 --> 00:07:51,000
who got her own daughter killed.

102
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:55,000
♪Good deeds bloom from lies♪

103
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,480
♪Who's next nailed to this wall?♪

104
00:08:00,279 --> 00:08:01,079
Ms. Song...

105
00:08:01,879 --> 00:08:02,680
Stop...

106
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:04,839
Stop it...

107
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,920
♪The Executer is never late♪

108
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:12,400
♪Every sin will be paid for♪

109
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,560
So-called retribution

110
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:17,360
is a judgment on human nature.

111
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:19,040
Beyond the law,

112
00:08:19,839 --> 00:08:21,680
there shouldn't be another measure.

113
00:08:21,759 --> 00:08:23,480
But someone wants to personally measure

114
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,720
the cracks in the human heart.

115
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:29,200
♪Hear the hymn of bones torn down♪

116
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,279
Qin Ming.

117
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,240
I asked you here today

118
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,759
so you could witness

119
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:38,080
the judgment of Song Yalan.

120
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:41,360
Qin Ming, I don't want to hurt you.

121
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:42,919
The poison on the paper money

122
00:08:43,240 --> 00:08:45,080
will only knock you out briefly.

123
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:56,520
♪The sunflower bows, reciting names♪

124
00:08:57,560 --> 00:09:01,160
♪Each petal is a solemn phrase♪

125
00:09:02,680 --> 00:09:06,120
♪And moonlight, forever fair♪

126
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:09,080
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

127
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:16,560
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

128
00:09:31,759 --> 00:09:32,559
Han Liang.

129
00:09:32,799 --> 00:09:34,879
I smell something chemical
on the first-floor landing.

130
00:09:34,919 --> 00:09:35,720
Come quick!

131
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,399
Qin Ming?

132
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:49,399
Qin Ming?

133
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,399
Hear a case, Detective Ming.

134
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:57,639
A ship is about to sink.

135
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,320
Only two pieces of driftwood on board.

136
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,799
But there are three of us.
What do we do?

137
00:10:04,879 --> 00:10:06,919
I... I can opt out.

138
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,559
What nonsense!

139
00:10:11,159 --> 00:10:12,200
The answer is

140
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,000
we can tie the two pieces together.

141
00:10:15,679 --> 00:10:16,480
That way, all three of us

142
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,720
can hold on to them.

143
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:19,240
No one will sink!

144
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,840
You're awake.

145
00:10:52,159 --> 00:10:53,039
How do you feel?

146
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,519
Keke?

147
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:58,960
Ms. Song?

148
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:00,440
They both pulled through.

149
00:11:00,879 --> 00:11:02,120
Niu's now in a children's welfare home

150
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,720
we often work with.

151
00:11:53,799 --> 00:11:54,600
Mom.

152
00:11:58,159 --> 00:12:01,440
I love you.

153
00:12:12,759 --> 00:12:13,559
Mom!

154
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,440
(Epinephrine injected.)

155
00:12:17,159 --> 00:12:18,159
(Prepare for defibrillation!)

156
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,360
(Defibrillation ready.)

157
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,799
Mom!

158
00:13:31,799 --> 00:13:32,600
(Qin Ming,)

159
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,960
(when you see this letter,)

160
00:13:35,759 --> 00:13:37,240
(I will be gone.)

161
00:13:39,039 --> 00:13:40,279
(This ten-year play)

162
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,799
(is finally coming to an end.)

163
00:13:44,879 --> 00:13:46,240
(I spent ten years)

164
00:13:47,279 --> 00:13:49,759
(turning my daughter's death
into a killing spree.)

165
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:52,799
(I called myself the Executer)

166
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,360
(and chose the most extreme path.)

167
00:13:55,639 --> 00:13:57,279
(But in the end, I never felt)

168
00:13:57,519 --> 00:13:58,960
(the satisfaction of an eye for an eye.)

169
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,919
(Qin Ming, when you stood before me,)

170
00:14:02,919 --> 00:14:05,000
(I finally understood something.)

171
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,720
(If I hadn't chosen this path,)

172
00:14:07,879 --> 00:14:10,440
(if I had trusted the police,
trusted the process,)

173
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:11,519
(Wen's death)

174
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:13,759
(might have been solved faster.)

175
00:14:14,039 --> 00:14:15,000
(But at least)

176
00:14:15,159 --> 00:14:17,120
(I wouldn't have created new wounds.)

177
00:14:17,279 --> 00:14:18,639
(The people I killed)

178
00:14:18,799 --> 00:14:20,159
(were all guilty.)

179
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,840
(But that doesn't give me the right
to judge them.)

180
00:14:22,879 --> 00:14:24,360
(The law didn't fail.)

181
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,279
(I gave up trusting it.)

182
00:14:26,639 --> 00:14:27,200
(In the end,)

183
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,559
(I became a perpetrator just like them.)

184
00:14:29,879 --> 00:14:32,159
(I used hatred as a passport)

185
00:14:32,279 --> 00:14:34,799
(and turned my pain
into others' deaths.)

186
00:14:34,919 --> 00:14:36,200
(I thought I had won.)

187
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,279
(But in truth,)

188
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:39,720
(I lost everything I had left.)

189
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,799
(Including that child, Jin Keke.)

190
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,039
(She did wrong.)

191
00:14:44,159 --> 00:14:45,679
(She's spent ten years atoning.)

192
00:14:45,879 --> 00:14:46,720
(And me?)

193
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:49,360
(I spent ten years creating more sin.)

194
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:51,919
(Qin Ming, don't be sad about me.)

195
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,320
(I deserve to die.)

196
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:54,960
(My only regret)

197
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,759
(is dragging her into this.)

198
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,039
(If you can,)

199
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,559
(please tell her for me)

200
00:14:59,799 --> 00:15:01,360
(that the mom was fake,)

201
00:15:01,639 --> 00:15:03,360
(but my regret is real.)

202
00:15:03,799 --> 00:15:05,320
(I owe her an apology.)

203
00:15:06,039 --> 00:15:06,879
(Goodbye forever.)

204
00:15:07,919 --> 00:15:08,720
Qin Ming.

205
00:15:10,679 --> 00:15:12,360
We used to write letters in school,

206
00:15:12,559 --> 00:15:13,600
remember?

207
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:16,720
I didn't reply to the last letter

208
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,320
you wrote me.

209
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:21,759
Actually, I did write back.

210
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:25,320
It was a cry for help.

211
00:15:25,919 --> 00:15:27,600
In that letter, I told you

212
00:15:28,039 --> 00:15:29,759
everything that had happened to me.

213
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:32,080
I told you I couldn't hold on anymore.

214
00:15:33,879 --> 00:15:37,279
I wanted you to pull me
out of the nightmare.

215
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:45,159
But I never had the courage to send it.

216
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,320
I knew...

217
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,600
we could never have a future.

218
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:52,639
Qin Ming.

219
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,639
(Police)
For the past ten years,

220
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,639
I've been having the same dream.

221
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:07,920
(Police)

222
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,000
Thank you.

223
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,960
(Serve the People; Police)

224
00:16:41,680 --> 00:16:46,240
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

225
00:16:46,680 --> 00:16:50,680
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

226
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:54,680
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

227
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:59,360
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

228
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,359
What are you doing there?

229
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:11,720
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

230
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:12,960
Let's go.

231
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:14,720
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

232
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:18,800
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

233
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:22,640
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

234
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:25,559
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

235
00:17:25,559 --> 00:17:26,160
Grandma!

236
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:29,400
Have a baozi.

237
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:31,119
Save it for yourself...

238
00:17:34,319 --> 00:17:34,960
Do I get one too?

239
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,160
Dad, you too.

240
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:38,559
Come on, look at me.

241
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:41,119
Three, two, one.

242
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,279
Mom!

243
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:53,240
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

244
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,079
That's hot!

245
00:17:54,279 --> 00:17:55,079
Mom!

246
00:17:55,079 --> 00:17:58,320
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

247
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,720
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

248
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:04,560
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

249
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,760
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

250
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:09,640
Smells good?

251
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,519
So good!

252
00:18:10,519 --> 00:18:14,080
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

253
00:18:14,720 --> 00:18:16,880
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

254
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,920
♪We stop here in this night♪

255
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:23,240
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

256
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:29,320
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

257
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:37,240
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

258
00:18:49,800 --> 00:18:55,960
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

259
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:04,240
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

260
00:19:10,359 --> 00:19:11,200
Jin Keke!

261
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,680
I thought you weren't coming.

262
00:19:16,319 --> 00:19:17,440
Congratulations!

263
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,960
You got into the same university.

264
00:19:20,599 --> 00:19:22,200
I checked again and again.

265
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:22,960
That quiet guy

266
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:24,680
is really not my type.

267
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:26,519
Qin Ming.

268
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:27,319
You're a bookworm

269
00:19:27,319 --> 00:19:29,480
who only knows cases and dead bodies.

270
00:19:29,599 --> 00:19:31,319
Don't lead our Keke astray.

271
00:19:31,359 --> 00:19:32,279
Don't worry!

272
00:19:33,279 --> 00:19:34,480
I won't lead her astray!

273
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,519
I'll protect her.

274
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:41,120
♪Back then, you and I turned away♪

275
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:43,319
♪Silence swallowed the sound of crying♪

276
00:19:43,319 --> 00:19:44,400
Time is running out.

277
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:45,400
We should go.

278
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:48,600
♪The fading warmth on your cheek♪

279
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:52,520
♪Chilled my soul to the bone♪

280
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,160
♪The forever we once promised♪

281
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,480
♪Shattered into dust in the wind♪

282
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:01,319
(There are no Executers in this world,

283
00:20:01,519 --> 00:20:03,720
only those who turn themselves
into judges

284
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:05,759
and those they destroy.)

285
00:20:06,039 --> 00:20:07,880
(The law's punishment may come late,)

286
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:11,279
(but it will never create
new criminals.)

287
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:22,110
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

288
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:26,980
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

289
00:20:26,980 --> 00:20:30,980
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

290
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:35,330
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

291
00:20:44,310 --> 00:20:48,220
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

292
00:20:48,220 --> 00:20:51,200
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

293
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:55,340
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

294
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:59,570
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

295
00:20:59,570 --> 00:21:04,290
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

296
00:21:04,290 --> 00:21:08,440
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

297
00:21:09,310 --> 00:21:13,090
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

298
00:21:13,090 --> 00:21:17,180
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

299
00:21:26,140 --> 00:21:30,350
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

300
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:34,690
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

301
00:21:34,690 --> 00:21:38,460
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

302
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:41,360
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

303
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:46,150
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

304
00:21:46,150 --> 00:21:50,800
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

305
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:53,060
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

306
00:21:53,060 --> 00:21:55,200
♪We stop here in this night♪

307
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:59,620
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

308
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:05,600
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

309
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:14,360
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

